    [
     "Ecocirnov and CRTNnvert chairs",
     "ECOCIRNOV chair (E. LEMELIN coordinator 2016-2021- SYMEVAD and MEL partners) aims to simulate impacts of management of household waste by local public authorities; CRTNNVERT chair (E. LEMELIN co-titular of CRTNNVERT Chair 2020-2024 · large consortium) contributes to modeling different treatment methods of CDW. Both projects aimed to develop decision-support tools based on the comparison of scenarios at the regional level.",
     ""
    ],
    [
     "USAR (INTERREG)",
     "“Using Sediment As a Resource” (€4.821 M; 2016–2020), involved partners from France, Belgium, England and the Netherlands. Mouhamadou Amar contributed as a technical consultant. The project addressed dredged sediment as a secondary resource and supported cross-border circular- economy pathways for sediment management, treatment, valorisation, and reuse.",
     ""
    ],
